Camera collider pushout add in updateGameCamera and snapGameCamera? Let's design:

For desired camera position, before floor:
```
let safeX = desiredX, safeZ = desiredZ;
for (const collider of world.colliders) {
  if (collider.low) continue; // shrine low should maybe allow camera
  const dx = safeX - collider.x; dz...
  const min = collider.radius + 0.9;
  if (dist < min) {
    const push = min / dist; safeX = collider.x + dx*push; ...
  }
}
```
But this pushes camera out of building footprint whenever camera is inside, keeping view but possibly jitter and clip through other stuff. Also when player near a building, target-to-camera line may cross; pushout camera to circle edge could still be on wrong side but okay. We don't know building height; when camera above roof (y>6), no need. We can check groundAt? The building height ~3-4.5, camera y typically 3-5, so pushout always. We can only apply if desiredY < 5.5. Camera y 4.6. Good. Buildings around. Shrine low:true skip. Barrow columns colliders small. Trees maybe not in colliders? colliders only addHouse + shrine + barrow pillars. Good. So pushout from houses.

Could also shorten camera distance if the line from target to camera intersects a house circle. Instead of pushout, compute ray-circle intersection in XZ and clamp distance. This is better: camera stays behind player but moves closer when wall between. Use circle colliders with radius. For each house, compute if segment from target (player) to desired camera intersects circle expanded by 0.45; find nearest t; if t<1, reduce camera distance to t*distance - 0.3. This avoids camera inside walls and keeps line clear. But awning not in colliders. We can add awning as collider? It shouldn't block player; but for camera only, add camera blocker list. Add to world API: `cameraBlockers` array with circles for awning/houses? Could reuse colliders for camera plus separate awning blocker. Add awning circle (x7.4,z13.5,r2.4) to a new array `cameraBlockers`, plus houses. But simpler ray-circle against colliders and awning separately by pushing awning into collider with `low:true`? low means skip for player and skip for camera if low. We can add property `cameraOnly: true` and include for camera. Let's not overcomplicate. Camera clipping is small.

Maybe biggest visual defect from current screenshot is only spawn occlusion; fix that. We'll not add complex collision now, but a modest collider-based camera distance clamp will improve houses. Implement in updateGameCamera:
```
let distanceScale = 1;
for (const collider of world.colliders) {
 if (collider.low) continue;
 // segment target->desired
 const rx = desiredX - target.x ...
 project circle center onto segment...
 if t in (0,1) and perpendicular distance < radius+0.6 and desiredY < 5.2 => distanceScale = min(distanceScale, max(0.25, t - 0.08))
}
```
But if player is next to building, the camera behind may intersect. This pulls camera very close (jarring) but better than inside. Apply smoothed desired? Camera lerp already smooths.

Also shrink only if camera y below building top ~5.5. Use `desiredY < 5.4`.

For snapGameCamera (respawn, load) apply same? It calls after teleport, but desired camera may be inside. Could refactor helper `cameraObstructionScale(target, yaw, pitch, dist)`. Simpler implement helper `cameraSafeDistance(target, dirX, dirZ, baseDistance, y)` returning distance. Use in both. But snap uses camera y computed. Let's write function and use.

```
function cameraClearance(targetX,targetZ,dx,dz,baseDist,camY) {
 let scale = 1;
 if (!world) return baseDist;
 for (const c of world.colliders) {
  if (c.low) continue;
  if (camY > 5.6) break;
  const ox = c.x-targetX, oz=c.z-targetZ;
  const t = (ox*dx+oz*dz)/baseDist; // since dir normalized
  if (t<=0.2 || t>baseDist) continue;
  const px=targetX+dx*t, pz=targetZ+dz*t;
  if (Math.hypot(px-c.x,pz-c.z) < c.radius+0.35) {
    scale=Math.min(scale, Math.max(0.3,(t-0.4)/baseDist));
  }
 }
 return baseDist*scale;
}
```
Where dx = sin(yaw)*cosPitch, dz=cos(yaw)*cosPitch, then actual distance along horizontal = distance*cosPitch; camY target.y+sin(pitch)*distance+0.2. The segment horizontal length = baseDist*cosPitch. Use horizontal coordinates. camera distance from target. t is horizontal distance. Obstruction scale = (t-0.4)/(baseDist*cosPitch).

Then desiredX = target.x + dx*clear? We need preserve vertical relative. Simpler compute factor f then use `distance * f`.

Implementation:
```
function cameraDistanceFactor(target, dirX, dirZ, baseDistance, camY) {
 const horizontal = baseDistance * Math.hypot(dirX,dirZ);
 if (horizontal < 0.5 || camY > 5.6) return 1;
 for colliders...
 const t = ox*dirX + oz*dirZ; // dir unit xz, t horizontal
 if (t < 1 || t > horizontal) continue;
 const perp = ...
 if (perp < radius + 0.45) {
   factor = min(factor, max(0.28,(t-0.6)/horizontal));
 }
 return factor;
}
```
Call after y computed, before desired vector. This makes camera zoom in near wall. Good. For awning add cameraBlocker? Could add awning position as a `cameraOnly` blocker in world.js colliders array with `low: true` but update loop skips low. We could add new `cameraBlockers` property including house colliders and awning circle. Add awning blocker. Let's just include awning in a new `cameraBlockers` array; but world construction addHouse pushes colliders. We can set api.cameraBlockers = colliders + awning circle? At end, `cameraBlockers` can be `[...colliders.filter(...), {x:marketX,z:marketZ,radius:2.6}]`. But colliders only houses. Fine.

However we can simply treat colliders, and reposition respawn. Good enough.

